==Strategy==
With a nasty [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]] and stronger threats, your first priority is to get rid of the unit cap to have an easier time. There's almost no income on the stage, so a Rich Cat is advisable at the start.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]] units are as helpful here as the [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|original floor 30]]. Notable examples are [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer]] and [[Calligraphy Cat (Rare Cat)|Tea Master]].
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] is amazing for taking out the more troublesome peons like the overbuffed Li'l Bun Buns in the stage. When the Li'l Bun Buns aren't on the field, he can deal chip damage to the boss aswell.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], when boosted by research combos, can hold the frontline reasonably well and create a near-impenetrable defense when aided by other meatshields. It comes from [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|a relatively easy advent stage]], too.
*[[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]], [[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]], [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]] and [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] are all wave shields that can actually outrange Masked Grandmaster Cat, making sure that he won't be able to release waves as long as they're alive. The latter may also freeze Masked Grandmaster Cat for short time.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]]'s [[Surge Attack|Surges]] can do a little chip damage, but the most important aspect is the [[Freeze]], stopping the boss for several seconds (and knocking it back in True Form) for you to catch your breath and kill off the peons. Doron's also extremely durable, ensuring he will never die before he unleashes his attack.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]], when timed and supported well, can deal fairly significant amounts of damage to the boss and is arguably the best rusher you could have here.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]] outranges the boss, while its Anti-Relic abilities and Wave Immunity can be put to good use and its LD hits the boss even if peons get in the way. Of course, it goes without saying you'll have to deal with the peons as well.
*Ubers are dependent on what you have. [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] are the most useful, expanding your selection of possible units if they can outrange the boss. Other Wave Immune Ubers, provided they outrange the enemies here, are likewise welcome, such as [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]] and [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Keiji]].

